---
title: "Examples"
description: "Find maintained qql-rs examples for Python, Node.js, WebAssembly, edge, geo search, medical retrieval, and SEC filings."
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

The repository examples are executable applications, not duplicated snippets
inside the documentation site.

| Example | What it demonstrates |
|---|---|
| `examples/python` | Python basics through advanced retrieval |
| `examples/nodejs` | Node.js parser and runtime APIs |
| `examples/wasm` | WASM parsing, planning, and browser-oriented APIs |
| `examples/edge-demo` | In-process edge execution |
| `examples/airbnb-demo` | Geo payloads and filtered search |
| `examples/medical-retrieval-ops` | Provisioning and retrieval operations |
| `examples/sec10k-qql` | Tenant-aware document retrieval |

Browse the [examples directory on GitHub](https://github.com/srimon12/qql-rs/tree/main/examples).

{% qqlExample title="Representative geo query" %}
```sql
QUERY TEXT 'quiet apartment near transit' FROM listings
USING dense
WHERE location GEO_RADIUS {
  center: {lat: 52.52, lon: 13.405},
  radius: 5000.0
}
WITH PAYLOAD INCLUDE (name, neighbourhood, price)
LIMIT 10;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

When adding an example, keep its QQL compatible with `language/v1`, document
the required backend and models, and provide a deterministic setup path.
